#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# polynomial_reduce

#% text
# `polynomial_reduce(p, [g1, ..., gk], [x1, ..., xm])` gives `[[q1, ..., qk], r]` with `p = q1 g1 + ... + qk gk + r`, where no term of r is divisible by the leading term of any gi.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The multivariate division algorithm in the lexicographic order of the variables x1 > x2 > ... (Cox, Little and O'Shea, section 2.3). With a Groebner basis as the gi the remainder is the normal form of p.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
polynomial_reduce(x^3 + y^3, [x - y], [x, y])
#% output
#= [[x*y + x^2 + y^2], 2*y^3]

#% cell
polynomial_reduce(x^2*y + x*y^2 + y^2, [x*y - 1, y^2 - 1], [x, y])
#% output
#= [[x + y, 1], 1 + x + y]

#% section
# See also

#% text
